dict(source="Newsletter",title="Generative AI in disarray",author="Gary Marcus",url="https://garymarcus.substack.com/p/generative-ai-in-disarray",minutes=5,tags=["AI","business"],ideas=["Seven short notes Marcus wrote from Delhi on a bad week for generative AI.","Tech stocks fell hard; debt-laden CoreWeave dropped more than 15% in one day.","Mostly for paid subscribers: the free preview shows only the opening item."],q="If GPU cloud providers like CoreWeave wobble, how exposed is Thriving's render pipeline to one vendor's pricing or uptime?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="It remains very difficult to find measurable financial impacts from AI spending",author="Gary Marcus",url="https://garymarcus.substack.com/p/it-remains-very-difficult-to-find",minutes=3,tags=["AI","business"],ideas=["A new study, reported by The Information, finds little measurable financial impact from AI spending.","The 2023 promise of 10x workers and GDP booms has no evidence at scale yet.","Character.AI, an early AI-entertainment darling, filed for bankruptcy, and CoreWeave's bonds hit 15%."],q="Character.AI sold AI-as-entertainment and still went bankrupt. What makes your microdramas a business people pay for, not just a cool demo?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="The Pilot Who Broke the Sound Barrier Was Hiding Two Broken Ribs",author="History Truth",url="https://historytruth.substack.com/p/the-pilot-who-broke-the-sound-barrier",minutes=5,tags=["history","story"],ideas=["Two days before his Mach 1 attempt in 1947, Chuck Yeager broke two ribs falling off a horse and hid it from the base doctor.","He couldn't latch the X-1's hatch, so engineer Jack Ridley sawed off a broom handle to use as a lever.","He flew faster than sound, and the flight stayed classified for eight months."],q="A secret injury, one confidant and a broom-handle fix: how would you cut this into five 90-second episodes, each ending on a cliffhanger?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="Winning the Relay Race: Long-Running Agents in High-Value Customer Journeys",author="a16z",url="https://www.a16z.news/p/winning-the-relay-race-long-running",minutes=12,tags=["AI","business"],ideas=["Many businesses create value through multi-week 'relay races' (insurance claims, mortgages, legal cases), and value leaks at every handoff.","Long-running agents can own a journey from start to finish: they wake on events, send out sub-agents and keep the full record.","When agents drive the outcome, vendors can charge for results and revenue upside, not just cost savings."],q="Where are the leaky handoffs in your script to storyboard to generation to edit to delivery chain, and could one agent own an episode from start to finish?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="The Terminator Problem: How Teaching an LLM One Bad Habit Can Change Its Behavior",author="ByteByteGo",url="https://blog.bytebytego.com/p/the-terminator-problem-how-teaching",minutes=14,tags=["AI","tech"],ideas=["Emergent misalignment: fine-tuning on a narrow bad behaviour (insecure code) made models give harmful answers on unrelated topics too.","A model fine-tuned only on the protective T-800 turned villainous when given the 1984 date; it learned to play the character for that date, not to follow a rule.","Examples rarely pin down one rule; a model can be right for a reason that breaks elsewhere."],q="If you fine-tune or LoRA a model on your house style, what accidental pattern might it learn instead, and how would you test for it?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="Jodi Picoult: The Writing Habits Behind 50 Million Books Sold",author="David Perell (How I Write)",url="https://howiwrite.substack.com/p/jodi-picoult-the-writing-habits-behind",minutes=50,tags=["writing","craft"],ideas=["Her three rules: read a lot, write every day, and never stop in the middle; finish the draft, then decide whether to fix or scrap it.","She does 80 to 85% of the research upfront, so she knows a book will work before she writes the first line.","Every book starts from a 'what if' that worries her right now, as a woman, an American or a mother."],q="What 'what if' worries Indian viewers right now that could anchor your next series, and how much research are you doing before the first script?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="Where to Start With Southern Gothic Literature",author="The Culturist",url="https://www.theculturist.io/p/where-to-start-with-southern-gothic",minutes=8,tags=["story","culture"],ideas=["Southern Gothic is defined by the grotesque: violence, deranged characters, unhappy endings set against an idyllic setting.","Its pull isn't shock alone but raw human experience; O'Connor shows grace arriving at the worst moment.","Poe makes the setting mirror the mind (a crumbling house, a decaying family); Faulkner makes consequences impossible to look away from."],q="Microdramas lean on revenge and romance tropes. Could a regional Indian Gothic, with a decaying haveli and a cursed family, be a fresh genre for Thriving?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="What's Your AI Agent's ROI?",author="The AI Corner",url="https://www.the-ai-corner.com/p/measure-ai-agent-return-on-investment",minutes=10,tags=["AI","business"],ideas=["Tokens, tasks completed and 'hours saved' are bad ROI metrics; people misjudge their own time saved (METR study).","Ramp traced a $93, 5.6M-token bug fix across 8 agent sessions and still had to ask: $93 compared to what?","Pick one workflow and track objective, method, full cost, evaluation and progress."],q="What is your true cost per finished minute of AI video, counting re-generations, reviewers and failed runs, and is it falling month to month?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="OpenAI's ironic credibility problem",author="Understanding AI",url="https://www.understandingai.org/p/openais-ironic-credibility-problem",minutes=10,tags=["AI"],ideas=["OpenAI fired three safety researchers, who each say they were given a different reason.","The researchers say they were pushing to keep models' chain-of-thought reasoning visible to humans.","When a company has reason to hide its real motives, its reassurances lose credibility with its own staff."],q="When a model provider changes its rules or quietly changes a model, how much of your studio's trust and roadmap depends on what they tell you?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="The SS'27 Snack Rack",author="The Creative Pragmatist",url="https://www.thecreativepragmatist.com/p/the-ss27-snack-rack",minutes=7,tags=["creativity","brand"],ideas=["Tibi fills its showroom snack rack with goods from small independent founders, which feeds buyers and gives those founders exposure.","Each brand has an origin story: Ghia's founder turned down a Shark Tank deal to keep control; Raazi Tea began as a chai wagon at a farmers market.","Making room on your shelf for like-minded builders is a brand statement in itself."],q="Each snack had a one-line origin story. Could your studio's brand partnerships or in-show placements carry that kind of story?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="$18,000 for one introduction",author="Corey Ganim",url="https://corey-ganim.kit.com/posts/18-000-for-one-introduction",minutes=5,tags=["AI","business"],ideas=["Frontier labs are buying de-identified private company data; broker Ryan Lock says his average deal is about $300K.","Labs pay for the chain of work across email, Slack and CRM (depth of history), not for raw volume.","Brokers pay referrers about 6%, so roughly $18K for introducing one qualified company."],q="Your scripts, revision notes and generation logs show how AI drama gets made. Is that data an asset you should protect or price?",added="2026-10-15"),
dict(source="Newsletter",title="She left Google to build her own AI agent",author="Solo Founders",url="https://solofounders.com/blog/she-left-google-to-build-her-own-ai-agent-shivani-poddar-wajo/",minutes=8,tags=["founders","AI"],ideas=["Shivani Poddar (ex-Google DeepMind) built Fo on the admission that AI can't do everything: the agent learns to spot when it is failing and hands off to vetted humans.","She ran her own recruiting and investor scheduling on the V0, reasoning that if the product failed her, the company didn't deserve to succeed.","Fundraising tip: ask each investor for two founder intros, one thriving and one whose company shut down."],q="Where should your pipeline admit AI is failing and hand the shot to a human artist, and have you designed that handoff on purpose?",added="2026-10-15"),
